Z||000000||Uaana||08-13-2000||12:03 AM||||Damn but I love hot summer weather! Went out for a short ride today before work and spotted an beautiful black 85GT? Also spotted another black coupe and a slightly used red coupe. all this in 30min.<BR>And to my fellow MN's any of you been out scaring the ricers in the Metro area? Pulled up at a light next to a riced out Altima complete with fart can exhaust and decided why not. So I drop the pass win and give a hand signal to the altima.. The kid just shakes his head no.. <BR>Standard you guilty?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||blayde8||08-13-2000||09:42 AM||||I've been seeing a lot of fiero's latley too.  I'm Standards brother.  Even though I don't have my license, when I see a ricer go by I just point at them and laugh.    <BR>   Standard left to go up to Duluth yesterday at 4:00 PM in his 86.5 GT, he has a mountain bike race, so I don't know if it was him.<BR>Keep on burning those ricers!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by blayde8 (edited 08-13-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||Standard||08-13-2000||06:33 PM||||Well I'm back!  I've been burnin' 'em where possible.. Just a few days ago I took out a last gen. Eagle Talon!  I looked over and there was a hot chick driving it.. she didn't look back, tho, and I didn't think she was gonna take off.  She started rolling forward before the light turned green so she already had about a half-car on me when she took off, and I wasn't expecting it so I didn't get the best launch, but I started pulling pretty good as soon as I hit third and ended up about a half-car ahead before I had to stop very quickly so I wouldn't miss my turn..  also took out an older Olds Tornado by about 3 or 4 carlengths up to 50.<P>The drive to Duluth was fun.. You ever been on hwy. 23?  2 lane highway, some nice curves, 55 mph limit and really rough in some areas.. it's a fun road at 80mph!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> don't worry guys, I had both hands on the wheel!  I made it from Mont-du-lac, about 144 miles north of my house (14 miles south of duluth) back home in an hour and 50 minutes!  hehehe.. Averaged about 80-85 mph and got 27 mpg to boot! I can't believe how wonderfully my GT is running.  Played traffic tag with a 98-99 Grand Prix and a newer Blazer.. they never got ahead of me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  of course, I didn't see a single fiero in the 140 miles that I went.. oh well.. also turned the odo over to 149,000.  almost to the big 1-5-0!!<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 148,000 miles and counting!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||14
